    <h1>Studiair<br />Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-meta">Established: [Effective Date] &nbsp;/&nbsp; Last Updated: [Last Updated]</p>

    <p>
      Kodai Kitaura (service brand: NOVERIS, the "Developer") establishes this Privacy Policy (the "Policy") regarding the handling of user information in the iOS app "Studiair" (the "App") as set forth below.
    </p>

    <h2>Article 1 — Overview of the App</h2>
    <p>
      The App is an iOS note-taking app that provides features for creating and managing handwritten notes, importing and viewing PDF files, and AI-powered handwriting analysis.
    </p>
    <p>
      Users can create and edit handwritten notes in the App, import PDF files into their library for management, and use the AI analysis feature to send selected handwritten areas to AI for summaries, organized content, and suggestions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Credits available in the App are required to use the AI analysis feature. Credits can be purchased through iOS App Store in-app purchases.
    </p>

    <h2>Article 2 — Information Collected</h2>
    <p>The Developer collects or stores the following information in connection with providing the App:</p>

    <h3>1. Account Information</h3>
    <p>
      When Users create an account or log in, the App collects the User's email address and display name. Email addresses are managed by Firebase Authentication and are generally not stored in Cloud Firestore. Display names may be obtained through Google Sign-In or Sign in with Apple.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a User uses the email privacy feature in Sign in with Apple, a relay email address generated by Apple may be collected.
    </p>

    <h3>2. Note Data</h3>
    <p>
      The Developer stores information related to notes created by the User in the App. This includes note titles, subject names, cover colors, background styles, handwriting stroke data, images attached to note pages, and other metadata necessary for creating, editing, and managing notes.
    </p>
    <p>
      Handwriting stroke data includes coordinates, colors, line types, and tool types of strokes, and is stored in JSON format or similar.
    </p>

    <h3>3. PDF Data</h3>
    <p>
      The Developer stores PDF files imported by the User into the App, PDF thumbnail images, and metadata required for PDF management.
    </p>

    <h3>4. AI Usage Data</h3>
    <p>
      When a User uses the AI handwriting analysis feature, the Developer may collect or store the image of the handwritten area selected for analysis, the text extracted by OCR, the date and time of the AI analysis request, token usage, credit consumption, information on whether the request succeeded or failed, and log information necessary for fraud prevention, incident investigation, and quality improvement.
    </p>
    <p>
      The App transmits only the image and OCR text of the selected area to external AI services, limited to what is necessary for AI analysis. The full text of the entire note, or note content not selected for analysis, is not transmitted to AI services.
    </p>

    <h3>5. Billing Data</h3>
    <p>
      For credit purchases and balance management, the App stores credit balance, credit purchase history, App Store transaction IDs, purchase date and time, purchase content, receipt data, and information required for purchase verification.
    </p>
    <p>
      Actual payment processing is handled through Apple's App Store in-app purchase system. The Developer does not collect credit card numbers, bank account information, or other payment method details from Users.
    </p>

    <h3>6. Information Stored on Device</h3>
    <p>The following information is stored solely on the User's device and is not transmitted to the cloud:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>UI background color</li>
      <li>Tool icon layout and display settings</li>
      <li>Handwriting tool settings</li>
      <li>Apple Pencil settings</li>
      <li>Note templates</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      However, if a cloud sync feature is introduced in a future update, this Policy will be updated in advance and Users will be notified as necessary.
    </p>

    <h3>7. Device and Environment Information</h3>
    <p>
      For the purposes of providing the App securely, preventing fraud, investigating incidents, and improving quality, the Developer may collect or record device type, OS version, app version, error information, request date and time, and technical information related to communications.
    </p>

    <h2>Article 3 — Purposes of Use</h2>
    <p>The Developer uses collected information for the following purposes:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Providing, maintaining, protecting, and improving the App</li>
      <li>User authentication and account management</li>
      <li>Storing, syncing, displaying, and managing notes, PDFs, images, and similar content</li>
      <li>Providing the AI handwriting analysis feature</li>
      <li>Providing AI-related features such as OCR processing, summarization, and suggestions</li>
      <li>Managing credit balance, purchase history, and usage history</li>
      <li>Purchase verification for in-app purchases, fraud prevention, and responding to inquiries</li>
      <li>Ensuring security, access control, fraud prevention, and incident investigation</li>
      <li>Reviewing usage patterns, and improving quality and features</li>
      <li>Responding to User inquiries</li>
      <li>Complying with applicable laws or terms</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Article 4 — Use of External Services</h2>
    <p>
      The App uses the following external services. Information transmitted to these services is handled in accordance with each service provider's privacy policy and other terms.
    </p>

    <h3>1. Google Firebase</h3>
    <p>
      The App uses Firebase Authentication, Cloud Firestore, Firebase Storage, and Firebase App Check.
    </p>
    <p>
      Firebase Authentication is used for user authentication; Cloud Firestore is used for storing note information, metadata, and credit information; Firebase Storage is used for storing note images, PDF files, and thumbnail images; and Firebase App Check is used for preventing unauthorized access and verifying that the App and device are legitimate.
    </p>
    <p>
      Primary cloud data for the App is stored in Google Cloud's Tokyo region or in the storage location configured in Firebase. For Firebase App Check, mechanisms such as Apple App Attest may be used to verify device and app legitimacy, and information necessary for verification may be transmitted to Google.
    </p>

    <h3>2. Google Sign-In</h3>
    <p>
      When a User logs in using a Google account, the App may obtain the email address, display name, and similar information necessary for login through Google Sign-In.
    </p>

    <h3>3. Google Cloud Vision API</h3>
    <p>
      As pre-processing for the AI handwriting analysis feature, the App may transmit the image of the handwritten area selected by the User to Google Cloud Vision API for OCR processing. Only the area selected by the User for AI analysis is transmitted.
    </p>

    <h3>4. Apple Services</h3>
    <p>
      The App uses Sign in with Apple, Apple App Attest, App Store in-app purchases, and Apple's purchase verification system.
    </p>
    <p>
      When a User uses Sign in with Apple, the display name, email address, or relay email address generated by Apple linked to their Apple account may be collected.
    </p>
    <p>
      Payment processing for credit purchases is handled by Apple. The Developer does not collect credit card numbers, bank account information, or other payment method details from Users.
    </p>

    <h3>5. OpenAI</h3>
    <p>
      The App uses OpenAI API to provide the AI handwriting analysis feature.
    </p>
    <p>
      When a User uses the AI analysis feature, the image of the handwritten area selected for analysis and the text extracted by OCR are transmitted to OpenAI API to generate summaries, organized content, suggestions, and similar outputs.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Developer does not transmit User personal information, full note text, or content not selected for analysis to OpenAI API beyond what is necessary for AI analysis.
    </p>

    <h2>Article 5 — Disclosure to Third Parties and Outsourcing</h2>
    <p>The Developer will not disclose collected User information to third parties except in the following cases:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>With User consent</li>
      <li>When transmitting information to or outsourcing processing to external service providers to the extent necessary for providing App features</li>
      <li>When disclosure is required by applicable law</li>
      <li>When necessary to protect a person's life, body, or property, and obtaining the User's consent is difficult</li>
      <li>When necessary to respond to fraud, security issues, or Terms violations</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      External service providers may include overseas companies such as Google, Apple, and OpenAI. User information may be transmitted to the countries or regions where these companies are located to the extent necessary for providing the App.
    </p>

    <h2>Article 6 — Security Measures</h2>
    <p>
      The Developer implements reasonable security measures to prevent leakage, loss, corruption, and unauthorized access to collected User information.
    </p>
    <p>
      The App employs HTTPS encrypted communications, Firebase Authentication-based authentication, access control via Firestore Security Rules, access control via Firebase Storage Security Rules, unauthorized access countermeasures via Firebase App Check, device and app legitimacy verification via Apple App Attest, rate limiting for AI analysis features, permission design to allow access only to the User's own data, and minimum necessary log management for fraud prevention and incident investigation.
    </p>
    <p>
      For the AI analysis feature, usage limits of 5 times per minute and 50 times per day are imposed as a general rule to prevent fraud. However, the Developer may change these limits as operationally necessary.
    </p>
    <p>
      While the Developer implements reasonable security measures, the security of information cannot be completely guaranteed given the nature of internet communications, cloud services, and device environments.
    </p>

    <h2>Article 7 — Data Retention Period</h2>
    <p>The Developer retains User information for the period necessary to provide the App.</p>
    <p>
      While a User continues to use the App, note data, PDF data, image data, AI usage history, and credit history are retained to the extent necessary for providing App features.
    </p>
    <p>
      When a User deletes their account, the Developer will delete data associated with the User, except for information required by law or for fraud prevention, accounting, or purchase verification purposes.
    </p>
    <p>
      Data subject to deletion includes handwritten notes, note metadata, handwriting stroke data, images attached to notes, imported PDF files, PDF thumbnail images, AI usage history, credit history, User-related files stored in Firebase Storage, and account information in Firebase Authentication.
    </p>
    <p>
      However, backups, logs, Apple-side purchase history, information required by law to be retained, and information stored on external services may not be immediately and completely deleted. In such cases, the Developer will promptly delete or anonymize the information within a reasonable scope.
    </p>

    <h2>Article 8 — User Controls</h2>
    <p>
      Users can manage their notes, PDFs, images, templates, and various settings through the App's features.
    </p>
    <p>
      Users can also request or execute account deletion through the in-app account deletion feature or through means designated by the Developer.
    </p>
    <p>
      Data subject to deletion cannot be recovered after account deletion. Please back up important notes and PDFs in advance as necessary.
    </p>

    <h2>Article 9 — Notice on AI Feature Use</h2>
    <p>
      The AI handwriting analysis feature in the App transmits the image and OCR text of the handwritten area selected by the User to external AI services.
    </p>
    <p>
      Users should take care not to transmit the following as AI analysis subjects: passwords, API keys, credit card numbers, bank account information, government-issued identification numbers such as My Number, highly sensitive personal information, information relating to the privacy of third parties, confidential information of schools, employers, or research institutions, and content of materials prohibited from disclosure or sharing.
    </p>
    <p>
      While the Developer endeavors to improve the safety of AI features, Users acknowledge that, due to the nature of AI features, output content is not always accurate, complete, current, or appropriate, and use them accordingly.
    </p>

    <h2>Article 10 — Billing and Purchase Information</h2>
    <p>
      Credits required for AI analysis and other features can be purchased through App Store in-app purchases.
    </p>
    <p>
      Purchase processing, refunds, and payment method management are subject to Apple's terms and procedures. The Developer stores App Store transaction IDs, purchase date and time, purchase content, receipt data, and information required for purchase verification for the purposes of purchase verification, credit allocation, fraud prevention, and responding to inquiries.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Developer does not collect credit card numbers, bank account information, or other payment method details from Users.
    </p>

    <h2>Article 11 — Use by Minors</h2>
    <p>
      Minors using the App must obtain consent from a parent or guardian.
    </p>
    <p>
      In particular, Users who make in-app purchases must obtain permission from a parent or the Apple ID administrator before purchasing.
    </p>

    <h2>Article 12 — Compliance with Laws</h2>
    <p>
      The Developer complies with the Act on the Protection of Personal Information and other applicable laws and regulations, and handles User information appropriately.
    </p>

    <h2>Article 13 — Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>The Developer may update this Policy as necessary.</p>
    <p>
      When this Policy is changed, the Developer will notify or announce the change to Users through in-app display, posting on the Developer's website, or other appropriate means.
    </p>
    <p>
      Updated Privacy Policy takes effect when posted within the App or on the Developer's website.
    </p>

